  "text": "The abstract best supports Hypothesis 4, though only in part. It says the review covers dust sources, \"primarily supernovae and asymptotic giant branch stars,\" plus interstellar medium reprocessing through grain destruction and growth, and it also discusses Red Super Giants, Wolf-Rayet stars, classical novae, Type Ia supernovae, and quasar winds. Hypothesis 4's claim that these sources, with ISM growth, can account for observed early-galaxy dust masses goes beyond the abstract, which only says the review will compare theoretical models with observations. The other hypotheses fare worse:\n\n- **Hypothesis 1** singles out primordial Type II supernovae as the primary driver and proposes MHD simulations with JWST and ALMA. The abstract names no such primary source and presents no such proposal.\n- **Hypothesis 2** describes a dual-mode model of obscured and unobscured star formation. The abstract doesn't address that split.\n- **Hypothesis 3** makes AGB-specific claims, including initial mass ranges, metallicity grids, and silicate, iron, and SiC dust compositions. The abstract mentions AGB stars only as one of several sources and gives none of these details.\n\nCHOICE: 4",
